/*
Package msg is everything brainfold says to a person, in every
language it ships. Msg names each message. locales/<tag>.txt holds
that locale's text, embedded by #load and parsed by jm:i18n when
the locale is put to use. English is the source and the fallback.

A message is one line, `key = text`. `key.one` and the other plural
forms are CLDR categories; a bare key is the other form. {0} to {9}
are arguments. Lookups allocate nothing.
*/
package msg

import "core:sync"

import "jm:i18n"

